00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:11.990
Horace, "Odes (Carmina)"

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.860
<b>Advanced Nurturing High School</b>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.050
Reporting in.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.640
<b>ANHS - Student Council Room</b>

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.000
I have the results of the first-years'

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.390
<b>Class 3-A
Student Council Secretary
Tachibana Akane</b>

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.190
special test on the isolated island.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.660
The winner was

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.550
Class D.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.050
Y-Yes...

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.360
<b>Class 3-A
Student Council President
Horikita Manabu</b>

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.800
<i>How will you clear your next challenge,</i>

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.860
<i>Ayanokoji?</i>

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.460
<b>Class 1-D
Ayanokoji Kiyotaka</b>

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.360
That man, your father, said this.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.990
"Someday, Kiyotaka will choose
expulsion of his own accord."

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:06.050
<i>"All human behavior is
goal-oriented," indeed...</i>

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.010
<b>2nd Season</b>

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.010
<b>Classroom
of
the
Elite</b>

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.450
Now <i>this</i> feels like summer break!

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.360
<b>Class 1-D
Ike Kanji</b>

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.360
<b>Class 1-D
Yamauchi Haruki</b>

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.630
You said it!

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.260
<b>Class 1-D
Sakura Airi</b>

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.970
<b>Class 1-D
Koenji Rokusuke</b>

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.580
Knock it off, Koenji!

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.580
<b>Class 1-D
Sudo Ken</b>

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.580
Damn it! Quit laughin'!

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.850
<b>Class 1-D
Horikita Suzune</b>

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:13.850
Horikita-san!

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.980
What are you up to?

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.980
<b>Class 1-D
Kushida Kikyo</b>

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.550
Isn't it obvious?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.480
Reading, huh?

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.960
It's not a romance novel, is it?!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.220
No.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.610
A lively day.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.270
Ayanokoji-kun.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.930
Would you like to join me for lunch?

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.250
<b>Class 1-D
Hirata Yosuke</b>

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:34.190
I'm meeting up with Karuizawa-san
and a few others...

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.960
No, thank you.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.610
What about just you and me, then?

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:45.060
No, I'd rather not get
on Karuizawa's bad side.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.620
Hirata-kun!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.870
I made it!

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.120
Ready to go?

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.870
<b>Class 1-D
Karuizawa Kei</b>

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.080
Karuizawa-san.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.310
Actually...

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.380
Do you mind if Ayanokoji-kun joins us?

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.810
Aww...

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:57.980
Forget that!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.880
I found the awesomest teppanyaki place!

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.410
<i>All students. Your attention, please.</i>

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.640
<i>The special test will begin shortly.</i>

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.550
<i>All students will receive
an email from the school.</i>

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.880
<i>Please check your phones and follow
the instructions found there.</i>

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.010
"Regarding the special test.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:26.180
Advanced Nurturing High School

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:25.930
Please come to the indicated
room at the indicated time."

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:35.670
All students,
Please come to the indicated room at the indicated time. Those who are more than ten minutes late may receive a penalty. Come to room 504 by 6:00 PM today.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:30.870
"Those who are more than ten minutes
late may receive a penalty.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.670
Come to room 504 by 6:00 PM today."

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.460
Enter.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.180
<i>Yukimura and the Professor?</i>

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.690
So it is revealed!

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.830
<b>Class 1-D
Sotomura Hideo</b>

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.190
One of the two final seats
was that of Ayanokoji-dono!

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.310
This is quite strange, isn't it?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.830
<b>Class 1-D
Yukimura Teruhiko</b>

00:04:58.570 --> 00:04:59.260
Yes.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.630
One more person is due to arrive.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.960
<b>Class 1-A
Instructor Majima Tomoya</b>

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.310
Please wait quietly until they do.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.500
Scuse me.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.660
What the heck?

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.120
What are you guys doing here?

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.220
You're late. Take your seat at once.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.670
Fine...

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.070
<i>She seems vaguely upset.</i>

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:36.190
I will now explain the special test.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.600
<b>Special Test</b>

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:42.830
The test will be administered
among eight discrete groups,

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.450
each named after a planet
of the solar system.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:50.430
Each group will include a sampling
of students from each class.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.120
Fourteen in total.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.110
Class C is in here, too!

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:58.310
Three from Class A, and Class B, too!

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.630
A-Aren't they our enemies?!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:07.530
We'll be acting not as members of Class D,
but as part of the "Mars" group.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:10.620
And our test result will be
assigned to the group as a whole.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.290
The testing period is three days long.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.390
There will be one day of rest in between.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:20.170
At 8:00 AM, the school will send an email

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.840
declaring one member of the group "the VIP."

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.960
<b>VIP</b>

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:27.140
Twice each day, a discussion
will be held within the group,

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.820
in which we will attempt to
discern the VIP's identity.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.830
Thirty minutes after the
sixth discussion concludes,

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.490
we will mail our answer to the school.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.300
Each person can send only one answer.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.050
However, the VIP themselves
is not allowed to answer.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:42.840
<b>VIP</b>

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.460
Um, "Case 1"...

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:50.410
If everyoneРІР‚вЂќaside from the
VIP and the VIP's classmatesРІР

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:51.780
<b>VIP</b>

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:57.410
<b>Same Class</b>

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.160
gets the correct answer,

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.000
all members of the group will be
gifted 500,000 private points.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.410
500,000 PPt

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.910
And the VIP will receive
an additional 500,000.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:00.520
<b>VIP</b>

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:00.520
<b>500,000 PPt</b>

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.400
F-Five hundred thousand?!

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.520
Then the VIP gets twice that? A million?!

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.280
"Case 2."

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.640
If at least one personРІР‚вЂќaside from
the VIP and the VIP's classmatesРІР

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:14.910
<b>VIP</b>

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:15.330
<b>Same Class</b>

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.740
fails to answer or guesses wrong,

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:18.750
the VIP will receive 500,000 private points.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.750
<b>VIP</b>

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.750
<b>500,000 </b>PPt

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:23.850
<i>Case 2 represents a scenario in which
the VIP keeps their identity hidden.</i>

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:29.130
<b>VIP</b>

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:28.620
<i>In this case, only the VIP
receives 500,000 points.</i>

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.130
<b>500,000 </b>PPt

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:34.660
But attempting to expose the VIP
before the test has concluded

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.560
will lead to a Case 3 or 4 result.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:41.490
In these two situations,
answers will be accepted

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:45.110
at any time of the day
during the testing period.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.790
Answers will also be accepted in the thirty
minutes after the test period concludes,

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:51.810
but in either case, wrong answers
will result in a penalty.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.240
"Case 3."

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:54.910
<b>VIP</b>

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.850
If someone other than the VIP emails the
school before the testing period is over,

00:07:54.910 --> 00:08:05.330
<b>VIP</b>

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.760
and gives the correct answer,

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:05.160
that student's class will
receive fifty class points,

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.770
and the one who gave the correct answer
will receive 500,000 private points.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.050
<b>500,000 </b>PPt

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:11.590
At this point, that group's
test will conclude.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.710
If the correct answer comes from
someone in the VIP's own class,

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:17.680
<b>VIP</b>

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:17.680
<b>Same Class</b>

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.290
their answer will be declared invalid,

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.780
and the test will continue.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.390
<b>Test Continues</b>

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:20.890
"Case 4."

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:21.560
<b>VIP</b>

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:25.510
If someone other than the VIP emails the
school before the testing period is over,

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:27.310
and gives an incorrect answer,

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:33.050
that student's class will
lose fifty class points,

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:37.250
and the VIP will receive
500,000 private points,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:37.200
<b>VIP</b>

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:41.540
<b>500,000 </b>PPt

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.910
while the VIP's class
receives 50 class points.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:41.520
<b>Same Class</b>

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:46.500
And the moment the incorrect answer is
received, the group's test will conclude.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.290
Additionally, if the incorrect answer comes
from someone in the VIP's own class,

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.930
their answer will be declared invalid
and will not be accepted.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:08:59.180
I see.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.810
You can email in your answer...

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.490
I'm not sure I followed all that...

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:08.190
I, too, feel rather bewildered...

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.130
I'll explain later.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.190
Don't bother the teacher about it.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:16.050
For this test, the school
will preserve your anonymity.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.800
After the test concludes,
only your group's result

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.580
and class-wide point changes
will be announced.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.080
What about the VIP's identity?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.590
It will not be announced.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:29.290
Neither will response status.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.590
It seems really hard!

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.840
Yeah!

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:36.380
<i>There are four clear test results.</i>

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:41.110
The whole group shares
the VIP answer and wins.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.590
<b>Class 1-B
Ichinose Honami</b>

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.350
<b>Class 1-B
Kanzaki Ryuji</b>

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:45.730
In the final response, at least
one person gets it wrong,

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.970
<b>Class 1-A
Katsuragi Kohei</b>

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.730
<b>Class 1-A
Totsuka Yahiko</b>

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.230
and the VIP wins.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:52.040
A traitor discovers the VIP.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.750
<b>Class 1-C
Ryuen Kakeru</b>

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.500
<i>And the final possibility...</i>

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:58.240
<i>There's a traitor, but they incorrectly
guess the VIP's identity.</i>

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.360
<i>"Thinking."</i>

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.820
<i>Analyzing the situation at hand,
clarifying all subjects at issue,</i>

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.290
<i>then going through a problem-solving process,</i>

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:09.370
<i>speculating and assigning new values.</i>

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.550
<i>Under these test conditions,</i>

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:14.090
<i>speculating on how others will act,</i>

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.710
<i>processing that, and influencing them...</i>

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:18.590
It sounds annoying.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:24.010
<b>2nd Season</b>

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:24.010
<b>Classroom
of
the
Elite</b>

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.140
It's almost time.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.140
Yes.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.650
<b>You Have a New Message</b>

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.650
<b>Sender: Advanced Nurturing High School</b>

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.650
<b>Cancel</b>

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.650
<b>Open</b>

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:35.030
I have the same message.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.380
It appears neither of
us was selected as VIP.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.780
This reduces our options.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:45.410
What do you think of this special test?

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.980
It largely depends on how
the VIP approaches it.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:51.920
Although I've thought of several
preliminary routes to victory.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.140
Impressive indeed.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.550
I look forward to your results.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.570
I'm also looking forward to seeing
where you take your group.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.300
Do you require my aid?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.470
No, thank you.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.680
And just so that I know,

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.330
the person you're most on guard for isРІР

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:09.940
Lovely weather, isn't it?

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.940
Why don't you let me join you?

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.190
Suzune, are you the VIP?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.690
You know I wouldn't tell you that.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.290
Or... would you tell me if I asked?

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.320
If you wished it, by all means.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.600
But let me ask you first...

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.710
How did you achieve that result
on the deserted island test?

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:35.830
Her reports showed no sign of
you taking any action at all.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.730
<b>Class 1-C
Ibuki Mio</b>

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.380
You think I'm stupid enough
to let her see through me?

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:42.330
She struggled against
me even when I was sick.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.660
How about a rematch, then?!

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.260
The result of the previous test...

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:51.480
It's not difficult to achieve,
when you know how it's done.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:56.330
But very few could come up with it and
execute it under those conditions.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.590
Not the kind of plan that an earnest
little girl like you could think up,

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.140
Suzune.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.750
Sorry to burst your bubble,
but I have no friends.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:09.120
Ayanokoji-kun over there is the
best I've been able to manage.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.610
Though he's such a bumbler,
I'd hardly call him a collaborator...

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.590
You must be tired of pathetic hangers-on.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.380
Don't take my picture!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.150
It's a little game.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:22.740
I'm going to find out who's
pulling your strings.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.370
Everyone, including your
hanger-on, is in my cross hairs.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.390
You seem awfully obsessed with Class D.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:33.550
I know the limits of what
Katsuragi and Ichinose can do.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.400
They're no threat to me.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:40.510
You're suddenly the woman
of the hour, Horikita.

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:43.620
And whose fault is that?

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:47.830
<i>The more they box her in,
the more eager she becomes to fight.</i>

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.850
<i>There's nothing to worry about here, I see.</i>

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.410
What now?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:53.990
Nothing.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:59.170
<b>Special Test
1st Discussion</b>

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.820
<b>Special Test
Mars Group</b>

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.800
This has to be the worst team ever.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.810
<b>Class 1-A
Machida Koji</b>

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.810
<b>Class 1-A
Takemoto Shigeru</b>

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.810
<b>Class 1-A
Morishige Takuro</b>

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.810
<b>Class 1-B
Hamaguchi Tetsuya</b>

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.810
<b>Class 1-B
Beppu Ryota</b>

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.310
<b>Class 1-C
Yamashita Saki</b>

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.310
<b>Class 1-C
Yabu Nanami</b>

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.820
<b>Class 1-C
Manabe Shiho</b>

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.690
Attention, everyone!

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.810
Why don't we start with introductions?

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:26.700
The school told us to do that, after all!

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.940
Is that really something
we need to bother with?

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:32.330
Let's leave it to anyone
who really wants to do it.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.370
Yeah, I guess I can't force you, can I?

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.710
But it's entirely possible
that the room is bugged!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:41.090
Well...

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:45.840
If that's the case, the people who don't
introduce themselves might be penalized.

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:47.840
I'll do it, then.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.220
Thanks!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:52.850
<i>Ichinose immediately takes the initiative.</i>

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.980
So, how should we go about this?

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:00.980
If you don't like the idea of me
playing moderator, let me know, okay?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.810
<i>And the way she brings that up...</i>

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:06.490
<i>Anyone who objects will be volunteering
to be moderator themselves.</i>

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:10.770
<i>And in the process of leading the
conversation, they may reveal too much.</i>

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.080
<i>Most will avoid it.</i>

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:17.610
Since I don't see any objections,
I'll moderate!

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:22.130
First, I think we should talk out any
aspects of the test that seem unclear.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.580
Does anyone have any questions?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:30.010
I guess I'll start, then!

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:34.010
I feel like we should try to
complete the test together.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:39.390
In other words, our best option
would be to go for Case 1.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:41.520
What do you all think?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.770
That's a no-brainer, right?

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.900
I'm in favor, naturally.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.260
Indeed!

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.260
Agreed.

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:49.530
I'd like to have more private points,

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.780
and I prefer to cooperate when I can.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.660
I'm <i>in</i> on this, baby!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.560
Who are you trying to be now?

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:57.670
We...

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:01.920
We of Class A have resolved
to abstain from discussion.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.570
A-Abstain?

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:09.930
For what purpose?

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.930
I guess I came on too strong, huh?

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:18.680
The simplest and most certain
way to benefit from the test

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.060
is to abstain from participation
from beginning to end.

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:24.130
<i>Instructions from Katsuragi?</i>

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:29.820
To refuse discussion and let the
unknown VIP run away with the points?

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.630
What is the least desirable test result?

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:34.860
Huh? Um...

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:39.600
Someone figuring out the
VIP and betraying everyone?

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.100
Precisely.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:45.460
The worst-case scenario results
from having a discussion,

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.290
someone suspecting someone
else of being the VIP,

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.710
and getting it wrong.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:53.580
I acknowledge the wisdom of
abstaining from discussion.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.720
But neglecting to identify VIPs

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:00.600
could heighten the point disparity
between the classes, couldn't it?

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:04.000
What if the VIP distribution
is extremely uneven,

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:07.730
with VIPs being overrepresented
within one class?

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.950
<i>Hamaguchi's concern is warranted.</i>

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:14.030
<i>Without knowing the class distribution
of VIPs among each group,</i>

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.330
<i>the abstinence strategy is
a difficult one to support.</i>

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.910
<i>But Katsuragi will have recognized
the mechanism behind it:</i>

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:22.090
<i>"Fairness."</i>

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:24.750
"Fairness for all classes."

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.170
This is a rule to which the
school scrupulously adheres,

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.260
and which was present in
the previous test, as well.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:32.860
I would expect an even distribution
of VIPs among the classes.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.010
You won't get all of them in one class.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.200
You... may be right.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:40.350
I think you guys make a great point.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.280
But actually carrying that out won't be easy.

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:45.910
You're betting on the fact that
none of the first-year students

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.770
will suspect or betray anyone else.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:51.030
Complete trust exists between
the members of Class A!

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.780
It does sound easier than
trying to find the VIP...

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.030
Might we perhaps accept their offer?

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:58.900
I see no reason to object.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:03.480
I just feel like Machida-kun's strategy

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:09.040
is one that Class A, specifically,
is incentivized to suggest.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.420
Am I missing a drawback to
leaving the answer hidden?

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:13.400
You're forcing the people of lower classes

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:16.550
to waste one of their few chances
at turning things around.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.050
That's...

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:23.420
A united front plan guarantees there'll
be no change in the final class rankings.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:27.060
Your plan involves a united front, as well!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.950
Not quite, actually!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:33.380
Our group contains four members
each from Classes D and C,

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:35.700
and only three each from Classes B and A.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:38.130
In other words, if we
achieve the Case 1 result,

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:43.450
500,000 PPt

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:43.450
Classes D and C each receive
500,000 extra private points.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.010
That's true.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:49.330
But wouldn't you be putting your own
Class B at a disadvantage, as well?

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:54.220
The alternative is possibly letting
Class A run away with the win.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:57.970
After all, the VIP might be in <i>your</i> class!

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.610
I agree with her.

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:01.130
<i>A fine counter-argument.</i>

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.630
<i>Class B must have discussed this in advance.</i>

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:14.500
One way or another, Class A's
philosophy remains unchanged.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.610
We will not participate in the discussions.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.990
Gosh...

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.200
What'll we do with them?

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:27.890
<i>No one can actually argue
with Machida or Ichinose.</i>

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:31.250
<i>Each class has their own schemes.</i>

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.550
Can we talk a minute, Karuizawa-san?

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.760
Hey. I've got a question for you!

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.140
What?

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:43.760
Did you have a fight with
Rika before summer vacation?

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.860
Huh? What?

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:47.510
Who's Rika?

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:51.160
A girl with glasses in our Class C!

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.610
She does her hair in buns.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.650
You don't know her?

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:56.390
Nope. Think you've got the wrong girl.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:00.030
She told us who it was!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.280
"A Class D girl with a ponytail" bullied her.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.250
She was waiting in line at a cafР“В©,

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:08.160
when someone shoved her aside to butt in!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.290
Yeah? Wasn't me.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:13.610
You don't remember?

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:16.880
If it <i>was</i> you, we'd <i>like </i>
to request an apology!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.920
You mind if we take a
picture so Rika can check?

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.630
Don't you dare take my picture!

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:23.970
What's with you?!

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.250
You might've broken her phone!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:28.790
Just tell the school and get a new one, then.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:31.100
I've got pictures and stuff on there!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.860
What's with you? What's the big deal?

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:36.820
If it wasn't you, why are
you being so pissy about it?

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.360
Just let me take the picture!

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.860
I said no!

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:40.940
What's your problem?

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:43.030
Look at her, playing the shy little girl!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.050
Are you kidding me?

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:45.870
I'll hold her. You take the picture!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:46.990
Cut it out!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.270
Hey. What's all this noise?

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.750
Machida-kun...

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.760
She's upset. Stop picking on her.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:01.330
S-Stay out of this, Machida-kun!

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:02.960
Do I need to call a teacher?

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.260
W-Well...

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.860
Let's go, everyone.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.140
S-Sure.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:11.940
Should we ask Rika again?

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.020
A picture would be faster, though...

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.070
Thanks, Machida-kun.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:26.890
<b>Special Test
Mars Group</b>

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:29.390
<b>Special Test
Second Discussion</b>

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:33.250
<b>Status:</b>

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:33.250
<b>Deadlocked</b>

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.970
I agree about the necessity of discussion.

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:38.170
We want to learn the identity of the VIP.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.420
But do you really think talking
is gonna bring that to bear?

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.760
This test is way too hard.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.030
I'd say it depends on our approach.

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:47.780
We could think of both this and

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:51.390
the island tests as, essentially,
a surprise for the students.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:52.890
Sunrise is my specialtРІР‚вЂќ

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.900
Isn't life aboard a cruise ship fun?

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:58.760
Even if we do have to attend these meetings,

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:00.900
we get to talk and use our
phones as much as we want.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:02.530
I guess.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.870
So why don't we just chat?

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:07.960
Staying in your shell all
the time gets stuffy, right?

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.640
You're free to enjoy yourselves as you wish,

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.760
but I refuse to trust you.

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:16.670
The VIP could be in Class B, as well.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.420
Can you trust your own comrades, Machida-kun?

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:22.550
Of course I can.
